==Trivia==
*Super Smash Families is a reference to [[wikipedia:Super Smash Bros.|''Super Smash Bros.'']]
**The event's Japanese name, Big Brawl Malevolent Families (大乱闘極悪ファミリーズ ''Dai Rantō Gokuaku Famirīzu''), instead references ''Big Brawl Smash Brothers'' (大乱闘スマッシュブラザーズ ''Dai Rantō Sumasshu Burazāzu''), the Japanese name of Super Smash Bros.
*The "Road" in both stages' names appears to be the result of a mistranslation. The Japanese names of [[Treacherous Road (Brutal)|Treacherous Road]] (悪逆無道 ''Akugyaku Mudō'') and [[Heinous Road (Brutal)|Heinous Road]] (極悪非道 ''Gokuaku Hidō'') are four-kanji set phrases that refer to extreme evil and roughly translate to "Heinous Injustice" and "Malevolent Cruelty", respectively, but the words 無道 ''mudō'' (injustice) and 非道 ''hidō'' (cruelty; inhumanity) contain 道, the kanji for "path", "way" or "road", which seems to be where the "Road" in the stages' English names comes from.

